msgstr "``FILE_ENVIRONMENT`` (implicit: ``/etc/environment``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``FRAMEWORK``: top-level ``meta/services.yml`` integration keys mapped to the in-axis target entity they wire the role into (the infinito-native, group-gated service flags), distinct from the curated upstream edges;"
msgstr "``FRAMEWORK``: nivel superior ``meta/services.yml`` chei de integrare cartografiate cu entitatea-ţintă din cadrul axei în care au transferat rolul (steagurile de serviciu infinito-native, gate-gated), distinct de marginile din amonte curatate;"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``False`` when the covered variant pins ``services.tor.enabled`` to a literal false, ``True`` otherwise. A reactive Jinja flag counts as capable: it is the role saying \"onion when the node is dark\". Consulting the variant matters -- roles pin the gate ``true`` in variant 0 and ``false`` in the rest, so reading only the base config claims an onion for rounds that deliberately run without one."
msgstr "``False`` atunci când pinii variantei acoperite ``services.tor.enabled`` unui fals literal, ``True`` Altfel. Un steag Jinja reactiv contează ca fiind capabil: este rolul de a spune \"ceapă când nodul este întunecat\". Consultanta variantei conteaza - roluri pin poarta ``true`` în variantă 0 şi ``false`` în restul, astfel încât citirea numai de bază config pretinde o ceapă pentru runde care rula în mod deliberat fără unul."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GH_TOKEN`` env var"
msgstr "``GH_TOKEN`` env var"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona şi afirmaţiile de referinţă sunt necondiţionate."

