# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "ejabberd's `mod_admin` HTTP UI is the only Playwright-testable surface; XMPP client login itself runs over 5222/5269 and MUST be exercised by an XMPP-aware client outside the Playwright test loop."
msgstr "Ejabard's `mod_admin` HTTP UI este singura suprafata testabila Playwright; XMPP client login se ruleaza peste 5222/5269 şi TREBUIE să fie exercitate de un XMPP- client conştient în afara buclei de testare Playwright."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "ejabberd's only HTTP surface is `ejabberd_web_admin` on `/admin` (see [`templates/configuration.yml.j2`](./templates/configuration.yml.j2)). It authenticates a bare JID against LDAP over HTTP Basic, so there is no Keycloak redirect to follow and no in-app logout control to click; client authentication itself runs over ports 5222/5269 and stays outside the Playwright loop, as noted under Watch Points. `acl.admin` additionally lists only the administrator JID, so the web admin refuses every other account outright. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the `guest` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "Singura suprafaţă HTTP a lui Ejabberd este `ejabberd_web_admin` privind `/admin` (Vezi? [`templates/configuration.yml.j2`](./templates/configuration.yml.j2))Acesta autentifică un JID gol împotriva LDAP peste HTTP Basic, astfel încât nu există Keycloak redirecționare pentru a urmări și nici un control de logout în aplicație pentru a face clic; autentificarea clientului se execută peste porturi 5222/5269 și rămâne în afara buclei Playwright, așa cum se menționează sub Watch Points. `acl.admin` În plus, enumeră doar administratorul JID, astfel încât admin web refuză fiecare alt cont pur și simplu. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) Prin urmare, declară `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` şi `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; `guest` Persona şi afirmaţiile de bază privind capacitatea de acces sunt necondiţionate."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "ejabberd’s ``mod_admin`` HTTP UI is the only Playwright-testable surface; XMPP client login itself runs over 5222/5269 and MUST be exercised by an XMPP-aware client outside the Playwright test loop."
msgstr "ejabard ``mod_admin`` HTTP UI este singura suprafata testabila Playwright; XMPP client login se ruleaza peste 5222/5269 şi TREBUIE să fie exercitate de un XMPP- client conştient în afara buclei de testare Playwright."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "ejabberd’s only HTTP surface is ``ejabberd_web_admin`` on ``/admin`` (see ```templates/configuration.yml.j2`` <./templates/configuration.yml.j2>`__). It authenticates a bare JID against LDAP over HTTP Basic, so there is no Keycloak redirect to follow and no in-app logout control to click; client authentication itself runs over ports 5222/5269 and stays outside the Playwright loop, as noted under Watch Points. ``acl.admin`` additionally lists only the administrator JID, so the web admin refuses every other account outright. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "ejabard ``ejabberd_web_admin`` privind ``/admin`` (Vezi? ```templates/configuration.yml.j2`` <./templates/configuration.yml.j2>`__). It authenticates a bare JID against LDAP over HTTP Basic, so there is no Keycloak redirect to follow and no in-app logout control to click; client authentication itself runs over ports 5222/5269 and stays outside the Playwright loop, as noted under Watch Points. ``acl.admin`` additionally lists only the administrator JID, so the web admin refuses every other account outright. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the ``guest`` Persona şi afirmaţiile de bază privind capacitatea de acces sunt necondiţionate."

